 "note": [
  "Rows are MEASURED, not reported: a verse is 'mined' only where the whole OLCB (lug_bib) verse text appears verbatim in the chapter (case and punctuation aside). Everything else is self_rendered, including the many Song of Solomon lines that keep OLCB's vocabulary but follow Taylor's AV/RV wording or line-breaks, because his exposition argues from that wording (e.g. 'a company of horses' 1:9, 'plaits of hair' 1:10-11, 'His banner over me was love' 2:4, 'until she please' 2:7 / 3:5 / 8:4, 'a very flame of the LORD' 8:6, where Taylor notes it is the book's only use of LORD).",
  "Taylor's bracketed glosses inside quotations are kept as he prints them (John 17:3 '(the object of)', 2 Corinthians 3:18, Song 8:6 '(ardent love)'). 'Song of Songs' is rendered from OLCB 1:1 (olusinga ennyimba zonna). LORD/CHRIST/FATHER in capitals are mirrored as MUKAMA/KRISTO/KITAFFE.",
  "The English 'Ps. xiv' (ch05) is Psalm 45:10-11 and is rendered as Zabbuli 45; see the PR for the English correction.",
  "AI-translated (job #6871) in one context, no fan-out; tag sequence identical to the English per chapter; awaiting native review."
